# NetProof environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` (docker compose reads it automatically) and fill in the
# REQUIRED value:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#
# Every value here maps 1:1 to an environment variable consumed by the server.
# The agent (agent/agent.py) consumes its own NETPROOF_* variables — see
# agent/README or the agent module docstring.

# REQUIRED. The dashboard admin password. The container refuses to start with
# an empty password so a default-credential deployment is impossible.
NETPROOF_ADMIN_PASS=change-me-to-a-long-random-secret

# Optional. Dashboard admin username (default: admin).
#NETPROOF_ADMIN_USER=admin

# Optional. Path to the SQLite database inside the container. Defaults to the
# persistent volume mounted at /app/backend/data.
#NETPROOF_DB=/app/backend/data/netproof.db

# Optional. Directory holding per-org guardrail YAML. Same persistent volume.
#NETPROOF_ORG_DIR=/app/backend/data/orgs

# Optional. Comma-separated origin allow-list for CORS. Leave empty (same-origin
# only) unless the dashboard is loaded from a different origin:
#NETPROOF_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://netproof.example.org

# REQUIRED for production TLS mode only.
# The public hostname for the dashboard. When set, start Caddy with
# "docker compose --profile production up -d" and Caddy will fetch a Let's
# Encrypt certificate for this domain automatically. DNS A/AAAA must point at
# this host on port 80/443 for the ACME challenge. Unset = plain HTTP dev mode.
#NETPROOF_DOMAIN=netproof.example.org